From: Abhi Teja Cholleti <achollet@qti.qualcomm.com>
Date: Thu, 13 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] pwhm: remove 6GHz automatic power-mode management

The automatic 6GHz power-mode management code (PowerType DM restore in
wld_rad_hostapd_setMiscParams and SET_6GHZ_PWR_MODE in the same function,
plus the post-channel-switch wld_rad_hostapd_set6GHzPowerMode call in
s_saveChanChanged) causes "Power mode change in progress" to be held for
the entire CSA countdown window (~420ms) when the parent AP changes the
6GHz channel along with a power-mode change (e.g. VLP -> SP/LPI).

During this window all CHAN_SWITCH commands to the 6GHz FH AP are
rejected, preventing mac80211 from creating the channel-context
reservation for wlan2.1/wlan2.2, which forces the BH STA to disconnect.

Also remove the dead //return; in s_chanSwitchStartedCb same-band path
since the return was already disabled in patch 0091.

Signed-off-by: Abhi Teja Cholleti <achollet@qti.qualcomm.com>
---
 src/nl80211/wld_rad_hostapd_api.c  | 24 ------------------------
 src/Plugin/wifiGen_eventHandlers.c |  4 ----
 2 files changed, 28 deletions(-)

--- a/src/nl80211/wld_rad_hostapd_api.c
+++ b/src/nl80211/wld_rad_hostapd_api.c
@@ -382,19 +382,6 @@
